            <div xml:id="d570">

                <pb facs="0700" n="598" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg598"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 10170/7.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Mexican Chargé to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >The Mexican Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1908-02-17"><hi rendition="#italic">February 17,
                        1908</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 138.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to the correspondence
                    exchanged between this embassy and the department in your worthy charge in the
                    extradition case of George Deering Reed, I have the honor to ask, by special <pb
                        facs="0701" n="599" xml:id="pg599"/> direction of my Government, that the
                    offender be transferred by the authorities of this country to Laredo, Tex.,
                    there to be delivered to the agents of my Government duly authorized to receive
                    him.</p>
                <p>I have pleasure in renewing, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">José F. Godoy.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
